# Settings for the kybr-alerting app (names only; values are Fly secrets and live in the private
# alerting runbook). Import with:  fly secrets import --app kybr-alerting
#
# --- Data source and delivery -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Fly read-only org token for the Prometheus API (the full "FlyV1 ..." string).
# FLY_PROM_TOKEN=
# SMTP relay host:port (STARTTLS), sender, username and password.
# SMTP_SMARTHOST=
# SMTP_FROM=
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# Where alerts go.
# ALERT_EMAIL_TO=
# Required: dead-man check URL pinged every 5 min by the always-firing Watchdog alert (the app has
# no Fly HTTP check, because both listeners are localhost-only).
# DEADMAN_WEBHOOK_URL=
#
# --- Thresholds (numbers; all required) -------------------------------------------------------
# Company lookups per slug in 15 min.
# T_LOOKUP_PER_SLUG_15M=
# Accepted verifications per slug in 15 min.
# T_VERIFY_PER_SLUG_15M=
# Cache reads per slug in 24 h.
# T_CACHE_READS_PER_SLUG_24H=
# Contact changes refused by the per-case limit in 1 h.
# T_CONTACT_LIMITED_1H=
# 429s per rate-limit policy in 5 min.
# T_429_PER_POLICY_5M=
# Shared-IP (ip-unknown) subjects per policy in 15 min.
# T_IP_UNKNOWN_PER_POLICY_15M=
# BFF key rejections in 5 min (internet scanners make this non-zero).
# T_BFF_REJECTED_5M=
# Provider calls failing (error or rate_limited) in 10 min, per call type.
# T_PROVIDER_ERRORS_10M=
# 5xx ratio over 5 min (0..1) and the minimum 5xx count before it fires.
# T_5XX_RATIO_5M=
# T_5XX_MIN_COUNT_5M=
